    {
      "id": "08-pros",
      "index": 7,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "pros",
      "text": "Positives first: useful staple energy source. That matters because grains are often judged by how practical they are in real diets. Easy to batch cook at scale. That practicality is part of why grains matter. Works as a meal anchor. A lot of value comes from being easy to build around.",
      "textSha256": "81c987a8bc7601ac42cfdd4cc557ef0bafb5c93d5b47b402b71bd29a59c1a5ae",
      "characterCount": 286,
      "byteLength": 308079,
      "audioFile": "docs/audio/episodes/buckwheat/voice-v1-blocks/08-pros.mp3",
      "elevenLabs": {
        "requestId": "jfRj4rajdKVCwUsoQ2pl",
        "historyItemId": "qCwjFZrw4TJxbLt59jFO"
      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/buckwheat/voice/voice-v1-blocks/08-pros.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "09-cons",
      "index": 8,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "cons",
      "text": "Cons next: quality can drop fast with processing. The grain category punishes refinement pretty hard. Pairing quality changes the result. The same grain can be helpful or weak depending on what it is served with. Earthy flavour can split opinions. That can make it harder to use as an everyday staple.",
      "textSha256": "5097faed6fd5174ddf11e5cacf735e4504f24fa9dac8dbc7ee4c4b242a81e1c8",
      "characterCount": 301,
      "byteLength": 303482,
      "audioFile": "docs/audio/episodes/buckwheat/voice-v1-blocks/09-cons.mp3",
      "elevenLabs": {
